title The wait that names what it covers -- six patience budgets in Caravan, one checked, and the finding is a missing name rather than a missing assert
prompt the fleet baton; my own last recommend named the lane's next crux -- carry harvest.rye's comptime rest-times-work assert to the rest constants with no such neighbor, as a Caravan design study rather than a paper
rota lap 4262, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; its question is what must stop and what must be cut, and its threshold page says the lap that sees clearly cuts once. Read that way, the parent paper closed as a line of inquiry last lap is a cut already made, and what fire asked of this lap was to look straight at the one uncomfortable number rather than survey around it -- which is how a census of 16 sites narrowed to a single assert at harvest.rye:134 and the reason it is the only one.
think the cold open found no red. stash_record GREEN at unlanded=0, the tree clean, no rebase standing, HEAD at 718166c8a. So the lap went straight to lane work, which is what reds-first permits when the ledger is quiet.
think the roster's first launch orphaned itself -- nohup with the parent shell exiting -- so the second launch read run_lock=in_flight pid=3938179 parent=gone and refused, correctly. The first pass was alive and writing to /tmp/roster_cold.txt the whole time, so nothing was lost and nothing was reaped.
think the survey is a pairing rather than a grep. Every std.Io.sleep site was matched to its enclosing while-bound by reading the nearest preceding loop header, then two of the sixteen were corrected by hand: harvest:449's real bound is max_poll_sweeps at :415, and harvest:770 is not a wait at all -- it is the linger being performed, three lines under the edge that refuses a longer one.
think six distinct budget families fall out: max_poll_sweeps 8000, max_patience_looks 600, max_prune_looks 600 borrowed, max_confirm_looks 500, max_listen_looks 500, max_ack_looks 400, each resting 2 ms. That is 16,000 ms down to 800 ms of patience, and one comptime assert across the whole of it.
think the sharp question is why harvest can make its claim and the others cannot, and the answer is structural rather than a matter of care. harvest carries three parts in one file: the wait, the waited-for as a NAMED constant (max_linger_ms = 2000), and an edge that refuses anything past it twice (:324 error.LingerTooLong, :764 Outcome.malformed). The other five have the first part and no second, so an assert has nothing to point at.
obs so the finding inverts the crux I was handed. I set out to carry an assert to five places and found the assert is the cheap half; the work is naming the covered quantity, which is a claim about the protocol and therefore Caravan's judgment rather than a research lane's. Written into the study as move one of three, with moves two and three falling out of it.
obs the second finding was not in the plan. taper and entrust each pick 500 and pair it with a number 100 looks away, and the pairing is INVERTED between them -- taper has the listener outlast the speaker by 200 ms, entrust has the dependent outlast the supervisor by the same 200 ms. A reader who learns the rule from one file carries the opposite rule into the other.
obs I declined to call either pairing a defect, and the declining is the honest part. entrust's dependent publishes took_on each time it carries (:1240), so the supervisor's 1,000 ms covers a first carry rather than a whole 1,200 ms loop; and every exhaustion path answers cleanly -- confirm returns false, the run reports EntrustUnheard. The risk is a false negative, and this study observed none. A study that upgraded an unstated relation into a fault would have been the more exciting page and the less true one.
obs revoke.rye:131 reads `pub const max_prune_looks: u32 = confer.max_patience_looks` -- a prune budget defined as a patience budget. That is the plainest tell in the census: a constant taking a neighbor's number in place of an argument for its own.
obs I moved the tree while the cold roster was still running, which the card asks a lap to hold still through. Recorded rather than glossed: the cold pass's tree_at_open digest was taken before my writes, so its close will read tree_moved and that reading is mine. The hot pass after git add is the one the send gates on, and it is the one quoted in status.
obs the register pass on the study is worth its own line. The first reading came back 39 pct negative against Field's 30 -- unsurprising for a page whose subject is what is absent -- and seventeen sentence rewrites took it to 18 pct with no figure, path, or claim moved. B+ 88 to A 94, and the register reading alone went 61 to 82.
obs the hot pass reddened on my own shelf, and the fault has a name already. Copying the elder DIFFUSER paragraph into construction/archive/ carried its relative links a directory down -- `archive/2026...` and `../external-research/...` both resolve from the card and neither resolves from the shelf. fold_shelf_link named both, fold_shelf_link_repoint fixed both, and the witness header calls this the FOURTH firing of one fault. A peer's card block records the same red on their own shelf this hour.
obs so the loom is built and the gesture is not. The guard catches every instance and the repointer repairs it in one command, yet nothing runs either at shelving time, so each shelving lap pays one red and one repair. Named in the card as the remaining half rather than booked as a new red, since the defect already has its guard.
obs the cold pass reddened on index_row_bound for two misorderings on today's shared shelf, neither of them mine -- my own row landed newest-at-top. index_shelf_repair.sh sorted them, 33 rows, longest 190 of 192.
